<title>USA: Kentucky House okays university spending increase.</title>
<headline>Kentucky House okays university spending increase.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFORT, Ky. 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kentucky's House of Representatives has approved Gov. Paul Patton's proposed $38 million spending increase for higher education.</p>
<p>The proposal passed 83-16 on Tuesday and now goes to the Senate. It increases funding by $10.5 million for the state's eight universities and by $11.7 million for its 14 community colleges.</p>
<p>It also provides $15 million of new funding for three incentive funds to encourage research and excellence at universities and improvements at technical schools.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
